    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Determine the number of separate operational/business units./organizations. This means the revenue generating operations of the program that will remain after program ending or separate business units that are operating under the program. In case of a franchise or connected operation falling under the same initiative you may aggregate the data and fill in one unit only _Calculate Net profit Margin as a Percentage: Net Profit margin = Net Profit ? Total revenue x 100. Net profit is calculated by deducting all company expenses from its total revenue. The result of the profit margin calculation is a percentage &#xfffd; for example, a 10% profit margin means for each $1 of revenue the company earns $0.10 in net profit. Revenue represents the total sales of the company in a period. Calculate over minimum of 6 months._</narrative>
    </description>
